{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher","id":10068,"title":"The Cipher","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T16:35:29-08:00","id":10068,"title":"The Cipher","content":"Let me start by saying that Demon the Descent is mind blowingly awesome. It has provided all the things I wanted in a Demon game, and many things that I never knew I wanted!<br /> <br /> With that said, let me jump right in to the concept of the Cipher. I love the concept of applying embeds to a cipher, needing to do them in order, and unlocking interlocks as you go. All this is leading to a deeper understanding of the Demon's personal Hell. <br /> <br /> Then, at the pinnacle of this journey they unlock the cipher itself which is....a sentence..<br /> <br /> I don't normally consider myself a power gamer, and I LOVE the idea that you get custom abilities as you unlock your cipher, but does it seem sort of...underwhelming...to anyone else that at the end of this awesome journey of self discovery you get a fortune cookie?<br /> <br /> I completely admit that I may be missing something, or looking at it from the wrong angle, and I am very interested in hearing other people's thoughts on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:39:01-08:00","id":10069,"title":"","content":"I was vaguely wondering if this should be some kind of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-13-2013, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:44:14-08:00","id":10076,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty limited view of the Cipher. Personally, I find the ultimate truth of the Cipher much more interesting than the interlocks that are earned along the way. The interlocks are a neat piece of candy to encourage the demon onward, as is the free Primum, but I enjoy the challenge of a personal revelation that clarifies and makes possible the demon's personal Descent. It's a pretty literal way of reading the text to think it must be a single sentence, or worse a fortune cookie. To my reading, it could be anything from a revelation of what the demon's inner search has been for all along and the path they must tread, to a secret and a road-map to the world without the God-Machine, depending on the demon's outlook and goals and the needs of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Now, all of that is pretty intimidating to come up with, especially individually for every PC in your game, and I think the game would benefit from spending more time expositing on the truths of the Cipher and samples of secrets unlocked past and future. But if you accept the challenge and try to make it work, I think it's a great idea. If you want to talk about techgnosticism, it's a little search for gnosis baked right into your character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:47:39-08:00","id":10077,"title":"","content":"The Cipher is tied to your Agenda. If you believe in a literal Hell, then your Cipher will help you find it. If you think Hell is a world free of the Machine, your Cipher can tell you something vital to achieving that. Fortune cookie it ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:38:08-08:00","id":10223,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll beg to differ: that\u2019s precisely what a fortune cookie <i>is</i> \u2014 or would be, in a setting where fortune-telling really works. That\u2019s why they\u2019re called <i>fortune</i> cookies.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, I agree with the original poster: while I get where atamajakki is coming from, I also found myself thinking \u201cthat\u2019s it?\u201d when I read what completing your Cipher gets you. I was expecting it to include some sort of state-change \u2014 probably not as drastic as even <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s Apotheosis, but maybe something that makes it easier for the demon to live \u201coff the grid\u201d: say, changing the fuel stat from Aether to Essence (thus permitting the demon to replenish its fuel stores from sources completely unrelated to the GM). Since the whole point of Hell is the absence of the GM, something of this sort would be a significant step toward achieving it.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019d really like to see, though, are a bunch of sample Interlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-14-2013, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:31:55-08:00","id":10262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=10223#post10223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll beg to differ: that\u2019s precisely what a fortune cookie <i>is</i> \u2014 or would be, in a setting where fortune-telling really works. That\u2019s why they\u2019re called <i>fortune</i> cookies.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, I agree with the original poster: while I get where atamajakki is coming from, I also found myself thinking \u201cthat\u2019s it?\u201d when I read what completing your Cipher gets you. I was expecting it to include some sort of state-change \u2014 probably not as drastic as even <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s Apotheosis, but maybe something that makes it easier for the demon to live \u201coff the grid\u201d: say, changing the fuel stat from Aether to Essence (thus permitting the demon to replenish its fuel stores from sources completely unrelated to the GM). Since the whole point of Hell is the absence of the GM, something of this sort would be a significant step toward achieving it.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019d really like to see, though, are a bunch of sample Interlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>from how I understand it that COULD be just what a cipher is giving you...the info of HOW to achieve that (and that fast enough to survive that^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T05:59:51-08:00","id":10354,"title":"","content":"Basically, the revelation you receive is a concrete step in the direction of Hell where before you were walking blind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:40:31-08:00","id":10360,"title":"","content":"We've had a couple of people ask for some sample Interlock as a stretch goal, and I think the idea is a good one. I wanted to put a bunch more in the core book and just ran out of space. If nothing else, this will get attention the Storytellers Guide, but I'd like to do something sooner than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:14:05-08:00","id":10530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=10223#post10223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll beg to differ: that\u2019s precisely what a fortune cookie <i>is</i> \u2014 or would be, in a setting where fortune-telling really works. That\u2019s why they\u2019re called <i>fortune</i> cookies.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the changeling game I just finished running there was a Goblin who had a special contract where he could reach into a vat of fortune cookies and give you one that actually told your fortune. And he was more than willing to teach it to you! For a price.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/200-totalworlddomination","name":"TotalWorldDomination","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:35:30-08:00","id":10550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=10360#post10360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had a couple of people ask for some sample Interlock as a stretch goal, and I think the idea is a good one. I wanted to put a bunch more in the core book and just ran out of space. If nothing else, this will get attention the Storytellers Guide, but I'd like to do something sooner than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the thing I want most from <i>Demon</i>.<br /> <br /> That and more <i>Pact </i>examples, because those are fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:48:32-08:00","id":10831,"title":"","content":"I wonder, though, how independent each demon's ciphers are supposed to be. If its supposed to be a cosmic secret, id imagine that the ST needs to connect the ciphers. for example, if a storyteller wants to play up on Hell being a place, would the storyteller still do a self-enlightenment style cipher for inquisitors? or would the ST tailor it more to the chronicle than to the character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:09:55-08:00","id":10953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=10831#post10831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, though, how independent each demon's ciphers are supposed to be. If its supposed to be a cosmic secret, id imagine that the ST needs to connect the ciphers. for example, if a storyteller wants to play up on Hell being a place, would the storyteller still do a self-enlightenment style cipher for inquisitors? or would the ST tailor it more to the chronicle than to the character?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be more of a personal choice or style consideration. I tailored Ciphers to the characters when I did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T12:45:56-08:00","id":17862,"title":"","content":"So correct me if I am wrong, but does the Cipher mean that the characters can only learn 4 embeds/exploits or is it possible to learn more, outside of the Cipher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T12:53:32-08:00","id":17867,"title":"","content":"They can learn as many Embeds and Exploits as they wish; unlocking an Interlock in a Cipher only implies trying to use two specific Embeds (aka Keys) together to learn a brand new, unique trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T12:56:02-08:00","id":17868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=17867#post17867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can learn as many Embeds and Exploits as they wish; unlocking an Interlock in a Cipher only implies trying to use two specific Embeds (aka Keys) together to learn a brand new, unique trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah cool, the whole cipher thing wasn't quite sinking in at first, it was confusing me a little. I honestly thought a demon could only learn embeds tied to the Cipher for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","user":"Jay Stewart","date":".  Because I suck at spelling. 11-25-2013, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:05:18-08:00","id":17875,"title":"","content":"It makes sense, I think. You are pretty much expected to start out with at least one Embed that has nothing to do with your Cipher; if you couldn't learn more unrelated Embeds after character creation, it would both be illogical and turn quickly into a silly guessing game with the ST. &quot;I thought I'd learn Ellipsis, now. Fits well with my character.&quot; &quot;Maybe, but it's not in your Cipher.&quot; &quot;Oh. Devil's Advocate instead, then? I like that one.&quot; &quot;Nnnnnnope.&quot; &quot;Okay, last time, it was Lucky Break you didn't allow me to learn... can I learn Animal Messenger?&quot; &quot;Hah, you're getting closer! But no, not that.&quot; &quot;You know what, screw the Cipher, I'm going to learn tons of Exploits instead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:10:38-08:00","id":17878,"title":"","content":"I do like how the cipher becomes a journey of self discovery that is tied to learning more about your supernatural side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:19:55-08:00","id":17893,"title":"","content":"It is! It's also a good incentive to me to ST a future game. I like designing that kind of stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Of course, once I do reach the point I'm STing a game and have to design Ciphers for the PCs, I'm likely to fall victim to artistic block, and throw my hands in the air, and ask what kind of evil I've done in a previous life for having to come up with tons of new powers while lacking all sense of balance... but that's the kind of thing that happens to me every time I ST anyway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:30:14-08:00","id":17900,"title":"","content":"Although it's something that's becoming a little difficult to explain to my players over Facebook lol. I'm looking forward to seeing if the Cipher gives players incentive to play past session one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T18:41:18-08:00","id":18077,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that the Cipher will get more attention in the Storyteller book, because, while I get that it's more than a fortune cookie, I'm a little lost as to how to implement it. I mean, once you get your Cipher, what's supposed to happen?<br /> <br /> I'm also slightly worried about what happens if a Demon PC ends up going in a completely different direction than the one the player and the ST envisioned at the beginning of the game. One assumes you should change the Interlocks and Cipher if necessary, but does that destroy verisimilitude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T11:36:39-08:00","id":18550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=18077#post18077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that the Cipher will get more attention in the Storyteller book, because, while I get that it's more than a fortune cookie, I'm a little lost as to how to implement it. I mean, once you get your Cipher, what's supposed to happen? I'm also slightly worried about what happens if a Demon PC ends up going in a completely different direction than the one the player and the ST envisioned at the beginning of the game. One assumes you should change the Interlocks and Cipher if necessary, but does that destroy verisimilitude?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not if you don't tell the players you changed them. Since the ST decides all of the Embeds and Interlocks in the Cipher after the first, the players have no way of knowing that what it ends up being by the time they unlock the whole Cipher wasn't what you had been planning all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T02:25:38-08:00","id":19054,"title":"","content":"Hm, am I the only one thinking it would be cool if the Cipher formed a diamond or circle, with the last and first keys interlocking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T08:38:57-08:00","id":19195,"title":"","content":"It is diamond shaped on the character sheet. I just looked at it again and realized that it DIDN'T have a final interlock between the last and first key. I agree, it should have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:48:31-08:00","id":20032,"title":"","content":"You could device a 4th Interlock, linking the first and last Key. The thing is that when you figure out the last key, you get 2 Interlocks, maybe +2 to Primum (you could rule otherwise here). So you kinda have to make sure that the 3rd isn't overshadowed by the 4th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T20:26:10-08:00","id":20048,"title":"","content":"Maybe the third Interlock could also confer a +1 to an Attribute or a lower level Demonic Form addition (Manifestation or Process) assuming you don't break up the last Primum bump that could be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T06:25:06-08:00","id":21140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=19195#post19195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is diamond shaped on the character sheet. I just looked at it again and realized that it DIDN'T have a final interlock between the last and first key. I agree, it should have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>God damn it, you're probably right. Grr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T09:40:19-08:00","id":21186,"title":"","content":"To some extent I got the impression that aspects of Demon might play well with Mage's Imperial Mysteries. You have an unbelievably powerful entity laboring through proxies to make alterations to the world and possibly reality itself. Certainly the God Machine is operating on that level. But then we have demons with their own struggle, bring about their vision of Hell, and getting these hints, as they perform what amounts to an arcane ritual in the form of Ciphers, that guides them toward making their vision of Hell a reality.<br /> <br /> Heck, there are even similarities in the terminology, Keys, Ascention/Descent, etc<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I read Imperial Mysteries and I haven't read Demon very closely, but the parallels didn't take any special effort for me to see.<br /> <br /> Ciphers being a guide as to how a Demon might participate in the Imperium, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T17:04:46-08:00","id":39695,"title":"","content":"I had the same thoughts.<br /> The Cipher Final Truth, needs to be a concete step towards your Hell.<br /> <br /> If, a realm hopping demon who has been searching for physical realm of Hell, then he realises logically &quot;A realm must exist, Where the god machine can not. It's antitisis.&quot; and gains the mechanical ability to start foring his equivlent of the Arch Mage's Road Across the Abyss to get there.<br /> <br /> If a Demon believes his hell must be built, hidden on earth, then he unlocks the ability to write his own bolthole merits, Eg Bolthole Size, Bolthole doors,<br /> <br /> THese are both First Concrete Steps, as it were.<br /> <br /> For the example given in the book of &quot;You realise the people must get mad to beak the status quo&quot;, you may take the Merit &quot;Allies: Angered Mob&quot;, all angered mobs will hear your points.<br /> <br /> However, remember when you unlock final secret you also unlock Interlock 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T07:19:36-08:00","id":42268,"title":"","content":"I am doing Ciphers for my group right now and I am having some difficulty with my Integrator. The player's concept is that his demon served as a messenger for various religious prophets over history, he was teamed with a Guardian who he eventually fell in love with. Most recently, he appeared and the Guardian was <i>not</i> there this time. He panicked and Fell.<br /> <br /> He ultimately wants to rejoin the Machine, but his priority is finding his lost love. I am having some trouble with his Final Secret, as I don't know how to give him a solid concrete step in the direction of rejoining the Machine when I as Storyteller don't know if that is possible yet.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas or suggestions to get me on track?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1283-duthuras","name":"Duthuras","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T08:00:54-08:00","id":42283,"title":"","content":"Okay, some ideas. Since love is a big motivator for him, I'd suggest making it an essential step in finding Hell (or, well, Heaven, depending how you look at it). You'll have time to figure out the specifics for reintegration. In fact, with the epiphany of the Final Secret may come the memory/knowledge of how to rejoin his old boss, and the details can be as esoteric as you want.<br /> - She was reintegrated, just like the cog she was, making her a part of It. Rejoin God, and you'll rejoin her, or, inversely, you'll find the God-Machine once you finally find her. Follow the breadcrumbs, and she will be in a Facility, waiting for you become another unthinking cog, just like her. =&gt; Love is where God is.<br /> - He has the possibility of giving away his freedom to his Angelic lover and make her Fall, with the knowledge he'll lose his and get back to the Machine and possibly forget what love even was. His choice. All he has to do is activate an Infrastructure with a special occult matrix so they can switch places... =&gt; Freedom is the grandest gift.<br /> - Trick the Machine into considering him a part of Its plans to the extent he'll need his own Guardian to protect you until he fulfills his task as a human pawn. It'll have to send back this specific Guardian for this. He may be accepted back if he completes the obscure mission without a hitch. =&gt; Before you can reach Heaven, you have to start out from Earth.<br /> - She's Fallen already, and is a Saboteur. Converting her will be very hard, even impossible. He'll have to choose between his love for her and his love for the Machine; the latter will contact him if he chooses to discard her. =&gt; You can have but one true love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 01-05-2014, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:42:16-08:00","id":42599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=21186#post21186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent I got the impression that aspects of Demon might play well with Mage's Imperial Mysteries. You have an unbelievably powerful entity laboring through proxies to make alterations to the world and possibly reality itself. Certainly the God Machine is operating on that level. But then we have demons with their own struggle, bring about their vision of Hell, and getting these hints, as they perform what amounts to an arcane ritual in the form of Ciphers, that guides them toward making their vision of Hell a reality. Heck, there are even similarities in the terminology, Keys, Ascention/Descent, etc It's been a long time since I read Imperial Mysteries and I haven't read Demon very closely, but the parallels didn't take any special effort for me to see. Ciphers being a guide as to how a Demon might participate in the Imperium, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had that feeling as well. It fits tier 4 style. The archdemon becomes the prince of his own private hell, a massive bolthole-realm out of the machine's grasp. Archmages probably are used to having to deal with archangels coordinating legions of angels to keep the peace and minimize damage to reality. Archdemons probably balance those archangels out, keeping them from annihilating all the elements of change that allow the Imperial Mysteries to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:56:59-08:00","id":44676,"title":"","content":"Maybe I missed something, but my main question about The Cipher is... WHAT is generating the Demons' Cipher? How is their sentence tailored so specifically to the Demon? Of course, that opens up a all kinds of neat possibilities, especially in a game about spying and paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:07:18-08:00","id":44936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=44676#post44676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed something, but my main question about The Cipher is... WHAT is generating the Demons' Cipher? How is their sentence tailored so specifically to the Demon? Of course, that opens up a all kinds of neat possibilities, especially in a game about spying and paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably an internal mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:11:22-08:00","id":44938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=44676#post44676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed something, but my main question about The Cipher is... WHAT is generating the Demons' Cipher? How is their sentence tailored so specifically to the Demon? Of course, that opens up a all kinds of neat possibilities, especially in a game about spying and paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets some attention in the Players Guide, but the short answer is, demons aren't entirely sure. Maybe it's all in their heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:55:50-08:00","id":45386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=44938#post44938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This gets some attention in the Players Guide, but the short answer is, demons aren't entirely sure. Maybe it's all in their heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>But The Cipher is always accurate, right? Or is that up for debate, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:58:59-08:00","id":45388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=45386#post45386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But The Cipher is always accurate, right? Or is that up for debate, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simon Flannery demonstrates that it's possible for demons to <i>misinterpret</i> their Ciphers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:58:55-08:00","id":45860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=45386#post45386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But The Cipher is always accurate, right? Or is that up for debate, too?</div> </div> </div> </div> If the storyteller is tailoring the cipher to each individual demon and their view of Hell, then every cipher can't be 100% true. My group's ciphers are all based on my headcanon, however, and what i've chosen to be Hell for my setting (Hell is inside archdemons). As such, theyre still tailored to the character, but do have an accurate hint on where the SL is going when tier 4 endgame comes around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:52:51-08:00","id":45986,"title":"","content":"Ciphers work by revealing unique capacities each Demon has by interlocking Embeds. The fact that Ciphers always seem to be tied to personalities and personal development is odd, but it's not like we haven't seen that sort thing before. The problem is how much are they tied? What is their connection to Hell? Are they connected or is that the Unchained are just transferring their obsession over Hell onto their personal development, (and by extension fulfillment)?<br /> <br /> Sure the others say it's a path to Hell, but can you really ever trust another Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T04:10:54-08:00","id":46166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=45860#post45860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the storyteller is tailoring the cipher to each individual demon and their view of Hell, then every cipher can't be 100% true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, the Word of Darkness' metaphysics are strange enough as to allow for apparently mutually incompatible phenomena and paradoxes. (If you doubt that, try to reconcile all the canon realms, dimensions, and worlds together. Or take a look at Mage's cosmology.)<br /> So, it could be that they're all true, even when Ciphers such as &quot;Hell is away from the G-M&quot; and &quot;Hell is close to the G-M&quot; exist in the same universe.<br /> That being said, I also like to think it's pretty much entirely a matter of interpretation and subjective point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T05:52:37-08:00","id":46192,"title":"","content":"Also, having gained a small bit of gnosis does not mean you understand the world fully. Two apparently contradictory visions of Hell can both be true when Hell is actually greater than both. Two demons with seemingly contradictory Hells talking about Hell might very well be the philosophical and metaphysical equivalent of two blind men describing an elephant they have touched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:55:20-08:00","id":47702,"title":"","content":"<i>Three blind men were led to an elephant and asked to describe it...</i><br /> <br /> Some might say that the blind men are the Demons, and the elephant is Hell, but I think that's too straight-forward.<br /> <br /> Others might say that the blind men are the players, and the elephant is having fun from the act of playing the game, but that's a bit meta for my taste.<br /> <br /> I would say that the blind men are the viewpoints of the Demons through their players, and the elephant is the Cipher that leads to Hell. Akin to the God-Machine's efforts of putting together Infrastructure into Occult Matrices to get Output, each Demon's Cipher should be (to think of the terms very loosely) a piece of Command Infrastucture on the Demonic Occult Matrix to get the Output of Hell. A puzzle piece, not the picture on the puzzle box or the completed puzzle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T16:05:24-08:00","id":63634,"title":"","content":"A few things are not clear to me about Ciphers.<br /> <br /> Firstly, what's a Demon *player* to do once he discovers his Final Truth? It seems like there is a very sudden change in game dynamics from a quite sandboxy mode where the Demon player is exploring his character to.. &quot;BHAM! You've unlocked the final achievement. Now lean back and let the Storyteller do the rest&quot;. I realise it's not that simple and that there is a lot more to good role playing that uncovering secret powers but the extent of this discontinuity seems very jarring to me. Beyond the story crafted by the Storyteller there doesn't seem much driving the Demon on his Descent once the Cipher is discovered, especially given how cryptic/obscure they seem to be.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it's not entirely clear to me how difficult it's meant to be to discover your Cipher. This is a spy-themed game so as I understand it actual combat is not likely to be happening all that often and one hit of lethal damage equal to your Primum is not typically life-threatening. Thus, instead of exposing yourself to danger and seeking out angels so that you can roll for hints about your Cipher, you might as well just try all of your Embeds in turn and heal yourself with On the Mend on by donning your Demonic Form in a safe and reclusive location. Rinse/repeat. The main limit on that would then be how many Embeds you have, which leads me to the third question.<br /> <br /> How hard is it to learn a new Embed? They are pretty cheap it seems - 2 points each. But do you have to do anything else? Like Vampires have to drink a drop of the blood of another Vampire that knows a discipline they want to learn. Is there a non-XP/role-playing requirement to get a particular Embed? If I want to learn Voice of the Machine do I have to spend a scene trying to intercept its signals, for example?<br /> <br /> Finally, as people above have mentioned, it's odd that the interlocks are arranged in the diamond pattern if there is no final interlock in fact. Blackhatmatt suggested above that maybe there was a different intention at some point... Would you be willing to share your thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T17:05:41-08:00","id":63652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=63634#post63634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, as people above have mentioned, it's odd that the interlocks are arranged in the diamond pattern if there is no final interlock in fact. Blackhatmatt suggested above that maybe there was a different intention at some point... Would you be willing to share your thoughts on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I continue to lament my lack of a proper drawing program, but I'm somewhat enamored of this way of looking at the matter:<br /> <br /> Alter the diamond such that the first Key is in the right corner and displace the Interlocks to be between each Key, still going clockwise.<br /> <br /> This places the Key corresponding loosely to one's Fall and the Key corresponding to the discovery of the final secret on the borders of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oni_(folklore)#Demon_Gate\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;northeast&quot; part of the diagram that corresponds to one's personal road to Hell.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  widdershins is the opposite of the direction i meant 02-05-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T17:14:13-08:00","id":63658,"title":"","content":"Have you looked into GIMP or Inkscape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T20:15:38-08:00","id":66220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=44676#post44676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed something, but my main question about The Cipher is... WHAT is generating the Demons' Cipher? How is their sentence tailored so specifically to the Demon? Of course, that opens up a all kinds of neat possibilities, especially in a game about spying and paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way that I explained it to a player: When you're an angel, you're a piece of something that's connected to a whole. Like a piece in a completed puzzle, what's on the face of the pieces combines into a single picture, so there's at least one side that defines you when you're connected. But the individual pieces also have to have sides in various irregular shapes that define what the pieces look like when they're not joined together. Everything that is a part of the whole can be separated from the whole, and there's got to be a shape that defines what it is like when it's disconnected. As an occult being created for a specific purpose, meaning permeates your entire being. Your natural state is more conceptual than corporeal. So when you are created, you are defined by your purpose to the God-Machine, but you've also got to have a &quot;shape&quot; that defines what your purpose is when you're disconnected. It's not something that you're aware of and it's probably not something the God-Machine specifically designs for you, any more than someone making a vase designs the shards that will exist when the vase is broken. But in order for you to exist as an occult being of Purpose, you had to have it to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","name":"Abaddon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T00:19:15-08:00","id":66301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=63634#post63634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things are not clear to me about Ciphers.<br /> <br /> Firstly, what's a Demon *player* to do once he discovers his Final Truth? It seems like there is a very sudden change in game dynamics from a quite sandboxy mode where the Demon player is exploring his character to.. &quot;BHAM! You've unlocked the final achievement. Now lean back and let the Storyteller do the rest&quot;. I realise it's not that simple and that there is a lot more to good role playing that uncovering secret powers but the extent of this discontinuity seems very jarring to me. Beyond the story crafted by the Storyteller there doesn't seem much driving the Demon on his Descent once the Cipher is discovered, especially given how cryptic/obscure they seem to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lean back and let the Storyteller do the rest&quot; isn't what I took from it, almost the opposite really. My read is that the 'Final Truth', despite the name, isn't the end or even the climax of a chronicle. It can be a transition point between Act 2 and Act 3. They've been searching until this point, developing their resources and finding clues, frequently on the run or looking constantly over their shoulder, but discovering the Final Truth tells them &quot;here is how you can win.&quot; If I get to that point when running a game, i'd probably connect the philosophical truth to something concrete, a new capability the demon now has like making pacts for other supernaturals' abilities or the ability to command crowds.<br /> <br /> Luke discovers his Final Truth at the end of Empire when he loses to Vader in the big climactic setpiece battle, but there's a whole movie after that where he's able to use his newfound wisdom and power to be proactive and prepared for round two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=42283#post42283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- She was reintegrated, just like the cog she was, making her a part of It. Rejoin God, and you'll rejoin her, or, inversely, you'll find the God-Machine once you finally find her. Follow the breadcrumbs, and she will be in a Facility, waiting for you become another unthinking cog, just like her. =&gt; Love is where God is.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSide note: this is cool. I've been trying to get a better grasp on Integrators and their motives, and I was trying to think of how you could frame this in a positive way. There could be a good Integrator-friendly arc in realizing that you Fell because you were not doing what a much, much wiser entity designed you to do, and accepting that you are not always in the right even when you feel wronged. This scenario would be especially interesting if they learned that their lover had Fallen separately but ultimately decided to reintegrate, though the PC doesn't necessarily know the details of why/the circumstances under which they made that choice. It would be an act of incredible trust, anathema to a demon, to take that leap of faith and reintegrate without being able to know what motivated them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T06:44:41-08:00","id":66443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=66301#post66301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSide note: this is cool. I've been trying to get a better grasp on Integrators and their motives, and I was trying to think of how you could frame this in a positive way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shameless plug for another post on angels and demon interactions to potentially help! <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/62013-the-authorities-angelic-endgames-and-tactics?p=62130#post62130\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...2130#post62130</a><br /> <br /> The struggle between Angels and Demons is one of Law VS Chaos. The Machine God likes order, upholding the status quo, etc, while demons tend to be more about individuals. Angels are organized, demons tend to have little organization beyond the local ring, and maybe a local agency... if you trust them. <br /> <br /> So, into this dichotomy comes the Integrators. Many of them want to rejoin the God Machine... but on their terms. They see that the God Machine does things like create Y2K to save the human populace. They see that for all its evils, its also impersonal. Maybe, they think, they could help improve the God Machine. Make it be more human friendly, see them individuals worth saving instead of just resources to tend. Maybe they think they can be connected again, become an angel, but also maintain free will - have the best of all worlds, rejoin their fellow angels without a war. Make the God Machine understand the idea that freedom and security need to be balanced, not one taken to an utmost extreme.<br /> <br /> To an Integrator, the God Machine is a necessary evil. However, they feel that it doesn't need to be evil, and could be made into the image of what humans see as an actual caring God.<br /> <br /> In the case of your particular Integrator, it seems he wants to rejoin the God-Machine in order to be free to embrace his love: going the Saboteur route would probably instantly knock him out of Integrator status, probably into Tempter camp. So, his motive is only to rejoin the Chorus; I don't think it sounds like he cares about the God Machine at all. Exile-hood could be a status he could enjoy as well, and get to be with his love, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T13:33:39-08:00","id":66689,"title":"","content":"&quot;Luke discovers his Final Truth at the end of Empire when he loses to Vader in the big climactic setpiece battle, but there's a whole movie after that where he's able to use his newfound wisdom and power to be proactive and prepared for round two.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get Final Truth a little better now. But could you possible provide a few more examples of the Final Truth and what it means in game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T20:24:01-08:00","id":66946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=66689#post66689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Luke discovers his Final Truth at the end of Empire when he loses to Vader in the big climactic setpiece battle, but there's a whole movie after that where he's able to use his newfound wisdom and power to be proactive and prepared for round two.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get Final Truth a little better now. But could you possible provide a few more examples of the Final Truth and what it means in game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider for a moment that the entire impetus of How An Angel Dies is Simon Flannery having completed his Cipher and drawn the complete wrong conclusion about what its final secret meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}